<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">County Waterford</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">County <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a> is a county in the province of Munster, in the south-east of Ireland, named after the city of Waterford, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> in the early 10th century. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its lands belonged to the Déisi, and the monastery of Lismore was one of Ireland's great schools. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Normans</a> took Waterford city in 1170, beginning the English conquest of Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/county-waterford.jpg" alt="County Waterford" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.geograph.org.uk/profile/10423 Mike Searle] · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castles_of_Munster,_Lismore,_Waterford-geograph-3038250.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
